CLAIM: On CUB K=29, lateroll averages 81.39% versus MaskedKD’s 80.22% on final seeds 1–3: +1.17 pp, paired 95% CI [+0.75, +1.58], at 12.9900 versus 12.9881 GFLOPs/img; no meaningful-gain or efficiency claim.
VERDICT: NEEDS-MORE
REASON: All six cited runs, including final_lateroll_k29_s1_1101_104303_ef38 and final_maskedkd_k29_s1_1101_104303_b676, support the reported numbers and have matching historical locks. However, actual locked-file diffs for faeb3cd, 8f67ca5 and bb22ead are missing: commit titles and diff statistics cannot establish unchanged training/measurement semantics. PROPOSALS and selector-creation history are also missing, preventing verification of the required analysis-before-implementation order.
The final parent advantage is +0.94 pp, not the request’s +0.50, and remains below 1.92; ToMe is explicitly flagged as budget-unmatched. Novelty is weak: the source implements a depth-restricted variant of existing [attention rollout](https://aclanthology.org/2020.acl-main.385.pdf). These results do not establish a promotion-worthy interpretability or FLOPs advantage.